sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-20--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-20--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2025-wisdom-20: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.47" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.475"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Site-appropriate regeneration after one drug is a direct anatomical comparison, and tail experiments have published summary indices. The paired tail-versus-leg scores required by the claim are not in a public file, and the limb result has not been released as an analyzable replicate set. Checking specificity in the cell collective requires those data." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Deliver the same systemic monensin treatment to animals with either a tail wound or a leg wound and score regenerate identity. Tails at tail wounds and legs at leg wounds would support specificity in the responding collective; identical structures at both sites, or no regeneration, would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Published tail regeneration indices are not a deposited animal-level dataset.", "The froglet limb series is not available as public raw counts or an independent replication.", "Systemic exposure has to be matched so that site differences are not dose differences." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2025-wisdom-20--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2025-wisdom-20 by Grok 4.7: 0.86" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
